## 3. MANDATORY SSOT READS (Proactive — No User Prompt Required)

Enforce all **28 Forensic Invariants (INV-1 to INV-28)**. Never rely on memory alone — open the SSOT before coding:

| When | Read (full SSOT) |
|------|------------------|
| ANY structural, domain, security, or migration work | [`.kiro/steering/forensic-standards.md`](.kiro/steering/forensic-standards.md) |
| Editing `lib/**/*.dart`, `test/**/*.dart`, or `supabase/migrations/**/*.sql` | [`.claude/rules/ci-blocks.md`](.claude/rules/ci-blocks.md) — apply all 20 CI block recipes |
| UI, E2E, Wasm async, auth lifecycle, golden tests, modal flows | [`.kiro/steering/lessons.md`](.kiro/steering/lessons.md) |
| OCC screens, penalty display, forensic reports, design tokens | [`.kiro/steering/ux-standards.md`](.kiro/steering/ux-standards.md) |
| New SQL migration | Also follow **Database Governance** in [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) + migration test plan under `forensic_records/plans/` |

**Code style, complexity gates, protocols, out-of-scope:** [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) — follow without duplication here.

---

## 4. WORKFLOW & PROTOCOLS

1. **TDD:** Write a failing test (`IntegrityException`) BEFORE writing implementation code.
2. **Step 0:** State Ponytail + consulted Skills (from `.agents/skills/`) and relevant Invariant Check (`INV-X`) before any code change.
3. **Integrity checks:** Run `make check` or `bash scripts/security/pr_full_scanner.sh` to ensure compliance before declaring a task done.
